            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anupama B R",
                        "email": "anupama.b.r1@ibm.com",
                        "username": "branupama"
                    },
                    "message": "this section is not clear, is only /system path should be published & ignore publishing remaining sub FRUs paths in system VPD collection flow ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Souvik Roy",
                        "email": "souvikroyofficial10@gmail.com",
                        "username": "souvik1914581"
                    },
                    "message": ">/system path should be published \n\nYes, that's why I mentioned \"system inventory path\". The rest of the paragraph covers the sub FRUs paths."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anupama B R",
                        "email": "anupama.b.r1@ibm.com",
                        "username": "branupama"
                    },
                    "message": "here not completely ignoring publishing other frus data, instead updating/resetting some of the properties value with default value right?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Souvik Roy",
                        "email": "souvikroyofficial10@gmail.com",
                        "username": "souvik1914581"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes. The following statement in the commit message explains this:\n\n>In\ncases of split mode system, file mode VPD will be enabled and system VPD\nwill be read from a file on the filesystem, so only the system VPD\nshould be published under the system inventory path and other sub FRUs\nunder the EEPROM containing system VPD should be published with default\nvalues."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anupama B R",
                        "email": "anupama.b.r1@ibm.com",
                        "username": "branupama"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/oem-handler/ibm_handler.cpp",
                    "line": 1402,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anupama B R",
                        "email": "anupama.b.r1@ibm.com",
                        "username": "branupama"
                    },
                    "message": "as API reseting other non 'system' sub FRUs, should API name be kept accordingly ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/oem-handler/ibm_handler.cpp",
                    "line": 1402,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Souvik Roy",
                        "email": "souvikroyofficial10@gmail.com",
                        "username": "souvik1914581"
                    },
                    "message": "Please suggest name."
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/oem-handler/ibm_handler.cpp",
                    "line": 1402,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anupama B R",
                        "email": "anupama.b.r1@ibm.com",
                        "username": "branupama"
                    },
                    "message": "resetNonSystemInvPaths, or resetDataOnNonSysInvPaths, clearNonSystemInvData \nclearDataForNonSystemPaths"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/oem-handler/ibm_handler.cpp",
                    "line": 1402,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Souvik Roy",
                        "email": "souvikroyofficial10@gmail.com",
                        "username": "souvik1914581"
                    },
                    "message": "\"NonSystemInvPaths\" can refer to all inventory paths other than system inventory paths, so can refer to other FRUs. Also this API is meant to function in Split Mode, so can't trim out \"SplitMode\"\n\nSince this API handles FRU containing system inventory path : \n\n`handleSystemInvSplitMode()`"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/oem-handler/ibm_handler.cpp",
                    "line": 1402,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "I agree with @anupama.b.r1@ibm.com to some extent.\n\na) \"SplitMode\" in the function name does not make sense as there is no constraint in the function which limit it to split mode. The method in itself reset the paths irrespective of from where it is called.\n\nb) \"UpdateSystemInv\" - It updates everything other than system inventory, which again is contradictory to what it does.\n\nAlso, I did not understand the below statement.\n\n> Since this API handles FRU containing system inventory path\n\n\nsystem inventory path is /xyz/openbmc_project_project/inventory/system, which is prefix of all the FRUs inventory path. So I did not understand what you meant by that sentence.\n\nAfter looking at the implementation, it looks like - it resets all the non system inventory path from the given input."
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/oem-handler/ibm_handler.cpp",
                    "line": 1402,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Souvik Roy",
                        "email": "souvikroyofficial10@gmail.com",
                        "username": "souvik1914581"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/oem-handler/ibm_handler.cpp",
                    "line": 1418,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anupama B R",
                        "email": "anupama.b.r1@ibm.com",
                        "username": "branupama"
                    },
                    "message": "can be kept out of the for loop, as consumer api sets value to zero at the beginning."
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/oem-handler/ibm_handler.cpp",
                    "line": 1418,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Souvik Roy",
                        "email": "souvikroyofficial10@gmail.com",
                        "username": "souvik1914581"
                    },
                    "message": "The variable is consumed inside the loop only. Why should we declare it outside?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/oem-handler/ibm_handler.cpp",
                    "line": 1418,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anupama B R",
                        "email": "anupama.b.r1@ibm.com",
                        "username": "branupama"
                    },
                    "message": "One advantage of declaring it outside the loop is avoiding repeated construction/destruction of the variable.\n\nSince l_errCode is reset by the consumer before being updated on each iteration, reusing the same object should be safe. However, I agree that its usage is limited to the loop body, so keeping it inside is also reasonable. Your call."
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/oem-handler/ibm_handler.cpp",
                    "line": 1418,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Souvik Roy",
                        "email": "souvikroyofficial10@gmail.com",
                        "username": "souvik1914581"
                    },
                    "message": "> One advantage of declaring it outside the loop is avoiding repeated construction/destruction of the variable.\n\nIt's just a `uint16_t` so not much gained by declaring it outside. Will keep it inside as its only required here."
                }
